from pathlib import Path
import csv,json
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]; out=root/'eco4o_slewfix'; scriptdir=root/'scripts/eco4o'
rows=list(csv.DictReader(open(out/'reports/sram_slew_before.csv'))); summary=json.loads((out/'reports/baseline_summary.json').read_text())
def table(headers,rs):return '| '+' | '.join(headers)+' |\n| '+' | '.join(['---']*len(headers))+' |\n'+''.join('| '+' | '.join(str(x) for x in r)+' |\n' for r in rs)
sections=[]
def sec(title,body):sections.append('## '+title+'\n\n'+body+'\n')
sec('1. Objective','ECO4O investigates and repairs 20 SRAM address/write-mask transition violations at 50 MHz. Closure requires zero setup, hold, capacitance and slew violations, legal placement, complete routing and extracted nine-corner STA. No constraints, RTL or SRAM source files are changed.')
sec('2. Starting Baseline','ECO4M ODB: `../eco4m_antennafix/soc_top.eco4m_drt.odb`.\n\nECO4M DEF: `../eco4m_antennafix/soc_top.eco4m_drt.def`. SHA-256: [baseline.sha256](reports/baseline.sha256).\n\nUser-supplied ECO4N reference: setup +1.5962 ns; hold +0.0876 ns; setup/hold/cap 0; slew 20. ECO4N is not a physical baseline. Fresh ECO4M ODB-derived STA independently gives +1.596245 ns setup and +0.087601 ns hold. Prior ECO4M/ECO4N state files reference an ECO4H logical netlist; this investigation exports its own netlist from ECO4M.')
sec('3. Tool / Environment Information','LibreLane 3.0.1 from `/nix/store/7z710dcbwpzq1xch9pa1xlm2yvn33s19-python3-3.13.9-env`. OpenROAD `26Q1-1989-g351788d062`. Standalone OpenSTA `3.0.0 83e1f9b77f`. PDK sky130A Ciel revision `8afc8346a57fe1ab7934ba5a6056ea8b43078e71`; sky130_fd_sc_hd; SRAM sky130_sram_1kbyte_1rw1r_32x256_8. Original config `../config_top_newcpu_eco4m_final_50mhz.json`. Scripts run actual local tools directly. Branch `backup-before-slim-20260709-221159`; pre-existing unrelated changes and .gitignore conflict are recorded in reports/git_status_before.txt.')
sec('4. Source of the 0.040 ns Constraint','[Full source audit](reports/constraint_source.txt). The effective 0.040 ns is an explicit bus-level SRAM Liberty max_transition at lines 188 (addr0), 225 (wmask0), 427 (addr1). It overrides the looser 1.500 ns SDC design limit. SRAM default is 0.5 ns; standard-cell default is 1.5 ns. This is not a LUT-index inference. SRAM measures 10–90%; standard cells measure 20–80%. All nine project corners use the same TT SRAM Liberty. No numerical relaxation is justified or applied.')
sec('5. Original Violating Pins',table(['Pin','Net','Driver','Driver Cell','Fanout','Cap (pF)','Distance (um)','Worst Slew (ns)','Limit (ns)','Corner'],[[r[k] for k in ['pin','net','driver_pin','driver_cell','fanout','total_cap','distance','sram_slew','limit','worst_corner']] for r in rows])+'\n[Complete CSV](reports/sram_slew_before.csv). Distance is Manhattan between average driver/sink pin geometry, not routed wire length.')
sec('6. Root Cause Analysis','All 20 terminal drivers are clkdlybuf4s25_1 delay cells on dedicated fanout-one nets. Their measured SS SRAM slews range 0.211623–0.265438 ns. Routed load and the 4/3 slew-threshold conversion worsen the terminal slew. There is no shared terminal branch to split. Original pin-to-pin distances are '+str(min(float(r['distance']) for r in rows))+'–'+str(max(float(r['distance']) for r in rows))+' um. buf_12 gives 0.042521 ns at a bare 0.00689 pF load with ideal input (standard-cell threshold), already above 40 ps before SRAM conversion. Inverters are faster, so this result does not prove library-wide infeasibility. Actual-SRAM probes show the need for more transition-restoring stages under load. Probe CSVs and raw logs are in iterations/top_newcpu_eco4o_feasibility/.')
sec('7. ECO Strategy','Preserve each existing delay cell to retain hold delay; add an even number of inverters to preserve logic polarity. A two-stage candidate was rejected by subsequent threshold-aware/load-aware probes before routing. Four-stage candidate: `existing delay cell -> clkinv_4 -> clkinv_8 -> clkinv_16 -> clkinv_16 -> SRAM`. A 400 ps source and 2 fF added load give 37.186 ps at the actual SRAM sink in an ideal-wire probe. This is a feasibility result, not post-route closure. All 20 share the same terminal topology; each is placed using its own sink coordinates and available legal row sites. Three pre-existing placement faults are repaired separately. Four-stage placement passed; the first uncongested-guide GRT attempt failed with overflow 339. Detailed routing is running with the same guides allowed to contain congestion; this is not a waiver of final DRC. Local spacer/decap removals are logged; these require physical verification.')
changes=[]
for p in sorted((out/'iterations').glob('top_newcpu_eco4o_*/changes.json')):
    if 'feasibility' not in str(p): changes=json.loads(p.read_text())
sec('8. Inserted Cells',table(['ECO Instance','Cell Type','Driven SRAM Pin','X (um)','Y (um)','Reason'],[[c['instance'],c['cell'],c.get('pin',''),c['new_xy'][0]/1000,c['new_xy'][1]/1000,c['reason']] for c in changes if c['action']=='insert']) if changes else 'No retained routed candidate yet. See iteration changes.json when placement completes.')
sec('9. Resized Cells','None. Existing signal-driver cell types have not been changed.')
sec('10. ECO Iteration History',table(['Iteration','Changes','Slew Vio','Cap Vio','Setup WNS','Hold WNS'],[['ECO4N reference','User supplied; not physical','20','0','+1.5962','+0.0876'],['ECO4M audited','ODB-derived netlist, original extracted RC','20','0','+1.596245','+0.087601'],['ECO4O-01','40 inverters; placement passed; threshold-aware probes reject candidate','Not post-route','Not measured','Not measured','Not measured'],['ECO4O-02','Four-stage candidate; see actual logs','Pending','Pending','Pending','Pending'],['FINAL','No accepted final implementation yet','Not closed','Not certified','Not certified','Not certified']]))
sec('11. Before vs After SRAM Slew',table(['SRAM Pin','Before (ns)','After','Limit (ns)','Final Status'],[[r['pin'],r['sram_slew'],'Not yet measured',r['limit'],'NOT CLEAN'] for r in rows]))
sec('12. Final Timing Summary',table(['Metric','Before ECO4O (user ECO4N)','After ECO4O'],[['Setup WNS','+1.5962 ns','No final'],['Hold WNS','+0.0876 ns','No final'],['Setup violations','0','No final'],['Hold violations','0','No final'],['Max cap violations','0','No final'],['Max slew violations','20','No final']]))
sec('13. MMMC Results','Fresh ECO4M ODB-derived baseline with original ECO4M RC; all nine corners executed:\n\n'+table(['Corner','Setup WNS ns','Hold WNS ns','Setup TNS','Hold TNS','Slew','Cap'],[[r[k] for k in ['corner','setup_wns','hold_wns','setup_tns','hold_tns','slew','cap']] for r in summary])+'\nThe TT-only SRAM model is reused as configured; this does not supply independent SRAM SS/FF characterization. Unannotated drivers are printed in full in raw STA logs and are not hidden.')
sec('14. Physical Verification','Original ECO4M check_placement fails: eco4k_d12_mid and eco4k_d13_mid are outside rows; eco_buffer_22 overlaps eco4k_a6_mid. [Original check](logs/export_baseline.log). ECO4O-01 site placement passes [check](logs/eco4o_01_placement.log); this candidate is not routed. ECO4M original DRT .drc file is empty, which does not establish complete geometry signoff. Existing ECO4M Magic extraction log independently reports 18 errors; its feedback.txt identifies illegal overlaps between obsli1 and locali. These remain unresolved for ECO4O until rerun. No ECO4O Magic or final DRC pass is claimed.')
sec('15. LVS','PHYSICAL REVISION: no accepted final ECO4O. LOGICAL REVISION: baseline export matches ECO4M ODB; no final ECO4O LVS run.\n\nODB/DEF sources are listed in section 2. Verilog: results/soc_top.eco4m_from_odb.v, exported directly. Final ECO4O ODB, DEF, GDS, PNL, SPICE: not yet accepted/generated. Never reuse ECO4H PNL for ECO4O. No LVS PASS is claimed; geometric illegal overlaps and logical revision mismatch are separate issues.')
files=sorted([p for p in out.rglob('*') if p.is_file()]+[p for p in scriptdir.rglob('*') if p.is_file()])
(out/'reports/artifact_manifest.txt').write_text('\n'.join(str(p.relative_to(root)) for p in files)+'\n')
sec('16. Files Created','[Complete file manifest](reports/artifact_manifest.txt). Workspace: eco4o_slewfix/{reports,logs,results,iterations}; scripts: ../scripts/eco4o/. Final ODB/DEF/netlist/SPEF/STA/DRC/LVS are not claimed until verified.')
sec('17. Scripts Used','\n'.join('- `../scripts/eco4o/'+p.name+'`' for p in sorted(scriptdir.glob('*')) if p.is_file()))
sec('18. Exact Commands Used','Commands actually executed (relative to project root):\n\n```bash\nopenroad -exit v3_hier/top/scripts/eco4o/export_baseline.tcl\nopenroad -exit -python v3_hier/top/scripts/eco4o/analyze_geometry.py\npython3 v3_hier/top/scripts/eco4o/run_baseline.py\npython3 v3_hier/top/scripts/eco4o/driver_feasibility.py\npython3 v3_hier/top/scripts/eco4o/probe_pairs.py\npython3 v3_hier/top/scripts/eco4o/probe_chains.py\npython3 v3_hier/top/scripts/eco4o/summarize_results.py\nopenroad -exit -python v3_hier/top/scripts/eco4o/eco4o_insert_pairs.py\nECO4O_ITER_DIR=$PWD/v3_hier/top/eco4o_slewfix/iterations/top_newcpu_eco4o_02 openroad -exit v3_hier/top/scripts/eco4o/eco4o_legalize_route.tcl\npython3 v3_hier/top/scripts/eco4o/write_documentation.py\n```\nThe baseline export writes its netlist before the expected original placement-check failure. Logs preserve failed candidate-placement retries. No hypothetical signoff commands are listed as executed.')
sec('19. Reproduction Procedure','Verify baseline.sha256, export matching baseline netlist, run geometry and baseline STA, then feasibility probes. Run insertion with a fresh ECO4O_ITERATION name and route with its ECO4O_ITER_DIR. The insertion script starts only from ECO4M. Executed extraction/STA and physical/LVS stages will be recorded after they finish; closure is not yet reproduced.')
sec('20. Rollback Procedure','Select `../eco4m_antennafix/soc_top.eco4m_drt.odb` and matching DEF explicitly in downstream tools; verify reports/baseline.sha256. ECO4O lives in separate paths. Do not delete or write ECO4M. Do not reuse a candidate ECO4O netlist with ECO4M extraction.')
sec('21. Remaining Problems','40 ps slew closure under routed RC is not yet proven. Existing ECO4M placement errors, incomplete SRAM PVT models, baseline parasitic-annotation warnings, prior Magic overlaps, DRC and revision-consistent LVS all require explicit disposition. No constraint relaxation has been applied.')
sec('22. Final Status','STATUS = NOT CLEAN')
(out/'ECO4O_SLEW_FIX.md').write_text('# ECO4O SRAM Slew Fix\n\n'+'\n'.join(sections))
print(out/'ECO4O_SLEW_FIX.md')
